<title>TRINIDAD AND TOBAGO: CRICKET-WEST INDIES V INDIA ONE-DAY SCOREBOARD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-WEST INDIES V INDIA ONE-DAY SCOREBOARD.</headline>
<dateline>PORT OF SPAIN, Trinidad 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scoreboard in</p>
<p>the second one-day international between West Indies and India</p>
<p>on Sunday.</p>
<p>West Indies</p>
<p> S.Williams lbw b Prasad		  3</p>
<p> S.Chanderpaul c Karim b Kuruvilla   12</p>
<p> B.Lara c Karim b Prasad		  0</p>
<p> C.Hooper c Ganguly b Kuruvilla	14</p>
<p> J.Adams not out			   35</p>
<p> R.Holder c Karim b Kuruvilla	   0</p>
<p> C.Browne c and b Kumble		  7</p>
<p> I.Bishop c Prasad b David	     31</p>
<p> C.Ambrose c Sidhu b David		4</p>
<p> F.Rose b David			     5</p>
<p> C.Walsh st Karim b Kumble		3</p>
<p> Extras (b-1 lb-2 w-4)		    7</p>
<p> Total (43.5 overs)		     121</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-5 2-5 3-32 4-32 5-32 6-44 7-100</p>
<p>8-107 9-116</p>
<p>Bowling: Prasad 8-1-22-2 (w4), Kuruvilla 10-2-23-3, Kumble</p>
<p>8.5-3-22-2, Ganguly 8-1-26-0, David 8-0-21-3, Tendulkar 1-0-4-0</p>
<p>India</p>
<p> S.Tendulkar not out		     65</p>
<p> S.Ganguly not out			 39</p>
<p> Extras (b-4 lb-3 w-4 nb-1)	    12</p>
<p>Total (for no wicket, 23.1 overs)  116</p>
<p>Did not bat: N.Sidhu, A.Jadeja, R.Dravid, M.Azharuddin,</p>
<p>S.Karim, A.Kumble, N.David, A.Kuruvilla, V.Prasad</p>
<p>Bowling: Ambrose 6-1-21-0 (nb1), Rose 7-1-31-0 (w1), Walsh</p>
<p>6-1-17-0, Bishop 4-0-36-0 (w3), Hooper 0.1-0-4-0.</p>
<p>Result: India won by 10 wickets after target was revised to</p>
<p>113 off 40 overs</p>
<p>Man-of-the-match: Abey Kuruvilla</p>
